>3139</fpage><lpage>3144</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12368447</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005150-Trujillo1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Trujillo</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Mauri</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Benazzi</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Comini</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>De Palma</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>The mycobacterial thioredoxin peroxidase can act as a one-cysteine peroxiredoxin.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>281</volume><fpage>20555</fpage><lpage>20566</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16682410</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005150-Jaeger2"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jaeger</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Budde</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Flohe</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Menge</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Singh</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Multiple thioredoxin-mediated routes to detoxify hydroperoxides in Mycobacterium tuberculosis.</article-title><source>Arch Biochem Biophys</source><volume>423</volume><fpage>182</fpage><lpage>191</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14871480</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005150-Stehr1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stehr</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hecht</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Jager</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Flohe</surname><given-names>L</given-names></nam